ttychatter C walkthrough
========================

1. Build the program
--------------------

    make

2. Store an API key
-------------------

Plaintext config:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key

Encrypted with gpg:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

3. Fetch model catalog
----------------------

    ./ttychatter --update-models

4. Browse/search/select models
------------------------------

    ./ttychatter --models
    ./ttychatter --models --search free
    ./ttychatter --models --model-type routers
    ./ttychatter --select-model

5. Create an input file
-----------------------

    cat > input.txt
    Explain what a Unix pipeline is in one paragraph.
    Ctrl+D

6. Send input and write output/session log
------------------------------------------

    ./ttychatter input.txt session.log

7. Resume the same session
--------------------------

    cat > followup.txt
    Give me a tiny example.
    Ctrl+D

    ./ttychatter followup.txt session.log

8. Attach files
---------------

    ./ttychatter -a notes.txt -a image.png prompt.txt session.log

9. Use loopback output
----------------------

    ./ttychatter --loopback prompt.txt session.log | less

10. Interactive mode with colon commands
----------------------------------------

    ./ttychatter --interactive session.log

    ttychatter> hello
    ttychatter> :models
    ttychatter> :attach notes.txt
    ttychatter> :memory
    ttychatter> :quit

11. Demo mode
-------------

Demo mode avoids network/API use:

    ./ttychatter --demo input.txt demo.log
    ./ttychatter --demo --interactive demo.log


Interactive parity commands
---------------------------

Start a line-oriented session:

    ttychatter --interactive my-session.log

Or resume by session name/path:

    ttychatter --resume my-session.log

Inside the prompt, use colon commands for local control:

    :list
    :rename research-notes
    :select-model
    :edit-memory
    :pending
    :quit

These commands are handled by ttychatter itself and are not sent to the AI.
